{"data":{"updated_timestamp":"12/11/2026 15:40:53","profile":{"player_id":"83150","last_updated":"12/11/2026 15:40","fullname":"Ahmed Daniyal","short_display_name":"A Daniyal","name":"Ahmed Daniyal","gender":"M","dob":"03/07/1997","date_of_death":null,"place_birth":"","nationality_id":"6","nationality":"Pakistan","nationality_short_code":"PAK","nick_name":null,"player_skill":{"id":"2","text":"Bowler","role":"Bowler"},"batting_style":{"id":"1","text":"Right Handed"},"bowling_style":{"id":"12","text":"Right-arm medium fast"},"writeup":"<p>Ahmed Daniyal is a Pakistani international cricketer, born in Punjab, who operates as an express right-arm fast-medium bowler and right-handed lower-order batter. Daniyal stands as another remarkable success story emerging from Pakistan's grass-roots tennis-ball cricket network and the acclaimed Lahore Qalandars Players Development Program. His rise to prominence is a classic testament to Pakistan's raw talent pathways, and it has not taken him long to become one of the most exciting pace prospects on the national selectors' radar.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Daniyal's senior international debut against Bangladesh in July 2025 was nothing short of a dream. He made an immediate impact by picking up 2 for 23 on his T20I debut on July 22, 2025, in Mirpur, drawing early comparisons to some of Pakistan's great speedsters by clocking speeds up to 146 km/h in his very first over.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>He further raised his stock on the pathway circuit during the ACC Men's Asia Cup Rising Stars in November 2025. Playing for the Pakistan Shaheens, he delivered a tournament-defining spell of 2 for 11 against Bangladesh A in the final, followed by a composed Super Over performance where he conceded just 6 runs and took both wickets to seal the championship and claim the Player of the Match honours.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>On the domestic and global franchise circuit, Daniyal has quickly become a trusted short-format weapon. After early career stints with the Lahore Qalandars and the Melbourne Stars in Australia's Big Bash League, his multi-format utility was on full display during the 2026 Pakistan Super League for the Quetta Gladiators.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>He turned in several spectacular performances, including a lethal 3-wicket haul against the Karachi Kings and a masterfully economical spell of 2 for 13 against the Hyderabad Kingsmen, proving to be an invaluable asset under Powerplay and death-overs pressure. He also represented the Lahore Whites with distinction during the 2026 National T20 Cup, showcasing a rapidly improving lower-order batting capability alongside his primary skills with the ball.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>The ultimate validation of his consistent performances across the 2025&ndash;26 season came following an impressive run for Pakistan A against the England Lions in the UAE, when the national selection committee rewarded the pacer with his maiden senior international ODI call-up for a high-profile home series against world champions Australia.</p>\r\n<br />\r\n<p>Solidifying his status as a vital component of Pakistan's white-ball future, the ultimate reward for his meteoric rise arrived in September 2026, when he was officially named to the Pakistan squad for the 2026 Asian Games in Japan.</p>","relation":null,"social_details":null,"trophy_cabinet":null,"majorteams":{"team":[{"id":"6","active":"1","is_primary":"true","is_international":"1","text":"Pakistan"},{"id":"294","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Faisalabad"},{"id":"513","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Lahore Whites"},{"id":"713","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Pakistan Shaheens"},{"id":"776","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Pakistan Television"},{"id":"1266","active":"0","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text":"Melbourne Stars"},{"id":"1511","active":"1","is_primary":"false","is_international":"0","text"